//? Title: Longest common subsequences from the producing table
//? Subtitle: Original ABCBDAB example, actual tie choices and independent optimality checks
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A common subsequence preserves order while allowing gaps. The full-table dynamic
program returns one optimal sequence, and tie choices can change which optimum
is returned. This report reads the library’s actual table and traceback rather
than rebuilding display evidence, retains the original character example and
distinguishes insertion/deletion distance from unit-cost substitution distance.
)

\toc

> Prefix optimality

Let C(i,j) be the longest common subsequence length of prefixes a[0,i) and
b[0,j). Empty prefixes have length zero. Equal last elements extend a diagonal
optimum; unequal last elements force at least one last element to be omitted:

$$C(i,j)=\begin{cases}0&i=0\text{ or }j=0,\\C(i-1,j-1)+1&a_{i-1}=b_{j-1},\\\max(C(i-1,j),C(i,j-1))&\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}$$
\alttext(The prefix table grows diagonally on equality and otherwise takes the larger neighboring optimum.)

Induction on total prefix length proves the optimum. Traceback takes a diagonal
on matching elements, otherwise the upper neighbor on ties and the left neighbor
only when it is strictly better. That deterministic rule chooses one optimum,
not all optima or a lexicographically smallest one. All inputs are integer
sequences; character conversion below merely represents these ASCII examples.

> A tiny actual tie

For a=(1,2), b=(2,1), both one-element answers are optimal. The native
upper-neighbor tie preference returns1. The concept diagram reads the real first
traceback move and result.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcs_tie.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lcs_trace({1, 2}, {2, 1});
    std::print("| actual prefix i | actual prefix j | actual move | actual table value |\n| ---: | ---: | " "--- | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &e : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.i, e.j,
                   e.move == dm::algorithms::LCSMove::Match ? "match"
                   : e.move == dm::algorithms::LCSMove::Up ? "up" : "left",
                   t.table[e.i][e.j]);
    std::print("\nActual selected sequence element {}; actual cells {}; actual moves {}.\n",
               t.analysis.sequence[0], t.analysis.work.cells,
               t.analysis.work.traceback_steps);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("corner", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual C(2,2)={}\nupper/left tie", t.table[2][2])).node(
        "up", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual first move: up\nC(1,2)={}", t.table[1][2])).node(
        "match", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual diagonal match\nselected{}", t.analysis.sequence[0])).edge("corner", "up").edge("up", "match").save_svg("build/lcs_tie.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual prefix i | actual prefix j | actual move | actual table value |
| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |
| 2 | 2 | up | 1 |
| 1 | 2 | match | 1 |

Actual selected sequence element 1; actual cells 4; actual moves 2.
\image(figures/lcs_tie.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual tie preference and selected match on two tiny integer sequences.)
\alttext(The native full-table traceback takes the upper branch at the corner and returns1; another optimal answer exists.)

> Original ABCBDAB and BDCAB

Retain the original strings and deterministic result BCAB. Native capture
exposes the exact table used to produce that output and the actual chronological
traceback moves. The figure draws the table once and overlays those real moves;
red points identify actual matching diagonal sources. Match letters spell the
answer in reverse along the corner-to-boundary path, or forward when those
matches are reversed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcs_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::string as = "ABCBDAB", bs = "BDCAB";
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::lcs_trace(std::vector<int>(as.begin(), as.end()),
                                  std::vector<int>(bs.begin(), bs.end()));
    std::print("Actual selected LCS: {}.\n\n| actual a prefix | empty | B | D | C | A | B |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               std::string(t.analysis.sequence.begin(),
                           t.analysis.sequence.end()));
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.table.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} |", i);
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.table[i].size(); ++j) {
            std::print(" {} |", t.table[i][j]);
            p.text(j, -double(i), std::to_string(t.table[i][j]), {31, 41, 55},
                   12);
        }
        std::print("\n");
    }
    std::vector<double> x, y, mx, my;
    for (auto &e : t.steps) {
        x.push_back(e.j);
        y.push_back(-double(e.i));
        if (e.move == dm::algorithms::LCSMove::Match) {
            mx.push_back(e.j);
            my.push_back(-double(e.i));
        }
    }
    auto last = t.steps.back();
    x.push_back(last.j - (last.move != dm::algorithms::LCSMove::Up));
    y.push_back(-double(last.i - (last.move != dm::algorithms::LCSMove::Left)));
    p.line(x, y, "actual traceback", {148, 163, 184}, 2).points(
        mx, my, "actual matches", {220, 38, 38}, 11);
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < bs.size(); ++j)
        p.text(j + 1, .7, bs.substr(j, 1), {37, 99, 235}, 14);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < as.size(); ++i)
        p.text(-.6, -double(i + 1), as.substr(i, 1), {22, 163, 74}, 14);
    p.size(850, 850).x_limits(-1.5, 6.5).y_limits(-8, 2).title(
        "Actual producing LCS table and traceback").x_label("prefix length of b").y_label("negative prefix length of a").save_svg("build/lcs_original.svg");
}
```
