| original first sequence length | original second sequence length | actual LCS length | derived insertion/deletion distance |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 3 | 3 | 3 | 0 |
| 3 | 2 | 2 | 1 |
| 3 | 3 | 1 | 4 |
| 3 | 3 | 0 | 6 |
| 3 | 0 | 0 | 3 |
\image(figures/lcs_distance.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Insertion/deletion distance derived from actual optimal lengths.)
\alttext(Five listed integer controls include equality, gaps, reversed order, disjoint values and an empty input; the formula is explicitly not unit-substitution distance.)

> Actual full-table work

The implementation evaluates n*m nonboundary cells and allocates(n+1)*(m+1)
cells, even for disjoint sequences. Traceback takes at most n+m moves and stops
as soon as either prefix is empty. Count-only analysis still needs the full
runtime table. Linear-space Hirschberg is a separate library method, not a
property of this implementation. The following deterministic integer controls
measure real cells and moves without wall-clock timing or a randomized
performance claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lcs_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y, moves;
    std::print("| original length per side | actual DP cell evaluations | actual traceback moves | actual " "LCS length |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int n : {8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
        std::vector<int> a(n), b(n);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            a[i] = i % 7;
            b[i] = (i + 2) % 7;
        }
        auto r = dm::algorithms::lcs_analyze(a, b);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, r.work.cells,
                   r.work.traceback_steps, r.sequence.size());
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(r.work.cells);
        moves.push_back(r.work.traceback_steps);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual cells", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "",
                                                          {37, 99, 235}, 4).title("Actual full-table work").x_label("length per side").y_label("DP cells evaluated");
    q.line(x, moves, "actual moves", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, moves, "",
                                                              {220, 38, 38}, 4).title("Actual selected traceback work").x_label("length per side").y_label("traceback moves");
    dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1).add(p).add(q).size(900, 800).title(
        "Actual producing work, with separate units").fit_panels().save_svg(
        "build/lcs_work.svg");
}
```
